    "body": "> We should also figure out better styling for smaller screens. \n\nFor [the JavaScript spec](https://javascript.spec.whatwg.org/) I added this to the HTML:\n\n``` html\n<meta content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\" name=\"viewport\">\n```\n\n…and then applied the following styles (after applying the generic WHATWG spec CSS) to make the whole thing mobile-friendly:\n\n``` css\nhtml { background: #fff; tab-size: 2; }\nbody { margin: 0 auto; padding: 0; max-width: 60em; border: 0; }\npre, code, a { white-space: pre; white-space: pre-wrap; word-wrap: break-word; }\n@media (max-width: 60em) {\n    body { padding: 0 .625em; }\n    .toc { padding-left: 0; }\n}\n@media (max-width: 30em) {\n    .toc ol, dd { padding-left: 1.5em; }\n    dd { margin-left: 0; }\n}\n```\n\nFor the HTML Standard there may be more that’s needed, but it’s a start.\n",
